      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "417a7e0e-f0f6-5a05-9189-3dc51c62e4de",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Chelidonium majus, Duranta, Stylophorum diphyllum\n- Plant classifications: Chelidonium, Verbenaceae\n- Compounds: Repenins\n- Topics: common names, taxonomy, relatedness, isolation\n\nFacts:\n- Chelidonium majus is a herbaceous perennial plant and the only species in the genus Chelidonium.\n- Chelidonium majus is commonly known as greater celandine, tetterwort, nipplewort, or swallowwort.\n- The name tetterwort can also refer to Sanguinaria canadensis.\n- Duranta is a genus of flowering plants in the family Verbenaceae.\n- Stylophorum diphyllum has a common name derived from Chelidonium majus, a closely related European plant with similarly shaped leaves and similarly coloured and shaped flowers.\n- Repenins are antioxidative coumarinolignoids isolated from Duranta.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
